Field Type Required Description <code>current_query</code> string yes The natural language query the user has just submitted <code>context</code> object or null no Additional information about the request. Currently only <code>context.user_id</code> is used <p><code>context.user_id</code> is the User Profiler identifier of the user submitting the query. When present, the user's interest keywords are used to personalise the suggestions. When it is missing, <code>null</code>, or does not match a known user, the suggestions depend on the current query only. Other fields in <code>context</code> are accepted and ignored. They are reserved for future use, such as a summary of the current query's results.</p> <pre><code>{
  "current_query": "What is there to do in Verona tonight?",
  "context": {
    "user_id": "user1"
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>An anonymous request can omit <code>context</code> altogether:</p> <pre><code>{
  "current_query": "Average rainfall in northern Italy"
}
</code></pre>

Field Type Description <code>next_queries</code> array of strings The suggested next queries, most useful first <pre><code>{
  "next_queries": [
    "Concerts in Verona this weekend",
    "Opera at the Arena di Verona",
    "Late night restaurants in Verona"
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p>The service asks for 3 suggestions and returns at most 3. It can return fewer: suggestions that are empty, duplicated, or identical to the current query (ignoring case and surrounding spaces) are dropped. Clients should not assume exactly 3 entries, and should handle an empty list.</p> <p>Recommendations are generated by an LLM, so the same request can return different suggestions on different calls.</p> <p>Response time is dominated by the LLM call and is typically in the order of seconds. Clients should use a generous timeout. The DataGEMS ingress allows up to 300 seconds.</p>
